services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied. Node1's boot configuration persistently includes audit=1, and a directly observed reboot produced a new boot identity with audit=1 present in the live kernel command line. The provider-wide restart protocol is coherent: it captures a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered node state, independently corroborated by lifecycle snapshots.","limitations":[]}
